        "original_id": "d9954a99-39e7-5061-a0fc-0e522e6df8d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pomeranian, Sporting Lucas Terrier, Japanese Spitz, Elkhound\n- Concepts: Spitz-type dogs, terrier type, dog breed standards, Pomerania, Fennoscandian hunting dogs\n\nFacts:\n- The Pomeranian, also called the Pom or Pom Pom, is a Spitz-type dog breed named after the Pomerania region in Germany and Poland in Central Europe.\n- The Sporting Lucas Terrier is a small dog breed of the terrier type.\n- Japanese Spitz breed standards vary around the world on the ideal size, but the breed is always larger than the smaller Pomeranian.\n- Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds in the Spitz type that are used for hunting elk or moose and other large animals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "feaaf1dd-f3a3-58a1-9714-c89f93db34e6",
        "text": "Page: Pomeranian (dog). Sentence: The Pomeranian (often known as a Pom or Pom Pom) is a breed of dog of the Spitz type that is named for the Pomerania region in Germany and Poland in Central Europe.\nPage: Sporting Lucas Terrier. Sentence: The Sporting Lucas Terrier is a small breed of dog of the terrier type.\nPage: Japanese Spitz. Sentence: There are varying standards around the world as to the ideal size of the breed, but they are always larger than their smaller cousins, the Pomeranian.\nPage: Elkhound. Sentence: Elkhounds are a group of Fennoscandian dog breeds belonging to the Spitz-type dogs and used for hunting elk/moose and other large animals.",
